Calculator — Working & Flow
Overview

A simple calculator that takes user input, processes mathematical operations, and displays the result.

Flow
User Input
    ↓
Button/Event Handler
    ↓
Update Calculator State
    ↓
Process Operation
    ↓
Calculate Result
    ↓
Update Display

How It Works
Input — User enters numbers and operators.
Event Handling — Button clicks are captured.
State — Numbers and selected operator are stored.
Calculation — The appropriate operation is performed.
Result — The calculated value is generated.
Display — The result is shown to the user.
Clear — Calculator state can be reset for a new calculation.
Example
25 × 4 =
   ↓
25 × 4
   ↓
100
   ↓
Display: 100

Main Components
HTML       → Calculator structure
CSS        → Styling and layout
JavaScript → Logic, events, state & calculations

